From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:30:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 39/46] hottyterm: the command palette has no default key

Ctrl+Shift+P (Cmd+Shift+P on the Mac) opened the command palette over
whatever ran in the terminal, so a program never got the key: plx,
whose vscode keymap opens its own palette with it as VS Code does,
showed the terminal's palette instead, and its Split Right split the
window outside plx. The key now reaches the program, as the tab keys
do since 'no tabs'. The palette stays in the GTK context menu and the
macOS View menu, and a keybind still gives it a key.

Upstream lines: one in hottytermDefaults in src/config/Config.zig, and
its comment.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/config/Config.zig | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/config/Config.zig b/src/config/Config.zig
index 824b37e9c..17646e3fa 100644
--- a/src/config/Config.zig
+++ b/src/config/Config.zig
@@ -7475,7 +7475,9 @@ pub const Keybinds = struct {
 
     /// hottyterm: no tabs, since plx has them, and windows and full screen
     /// are the window manager's: no default keys for tabs, for quitting,
-    /// for closing windows or for full screen, on the Mac too.
+    /// for closing windows or for full screen, on the Mac too. The command
+    /// palette has no default key either, so its key reaches the program
+    /// (plx can open its own palette with it); the menus still open it.
     fn hottytermDefaults(set: *inputpkg.Binding.Set, alloc: Allocator) !void {
         var drop: std.ArrayList(inputpkg.Binding.Trigger) = .empty;
         defer drop.deinit(alloc);
@@ -7500,6 +7502,7 @@ pub const Keybinds = struct {
                 .close_all_windows,
                 .quit,
                 .toggle_fullscreen,
+                .toggle_command_palette,
                 => true,
                 else => false,
             };
